From 423fe26edca96ac649537e888753e6fc582e665f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Hideyuki Nagase <hideyukn@microsoft.com>
Date: Sat, 30 May 2020 06:02:08 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 3/3] Rebase RDP-RAIL support from microsoft's mirror

I call this a rebase, but it also includes fixes to make it build,
and a general merge of many parts trying to reduce the ammout of
duplicated code.

This PR includes all (if not, it's a rebase mistake) changes since the original commit:
"Merged PR 4742168: Add preliminary RDP-RAIL support for weston"
https://github.com/microsoft/weston-mirror/commit/f590a956c378eb2ab765d05cb2331386f19f8704
up to
https://github.com/microsoft/weston-mirror/commit/f227edd681479ec3cb2290a25d84d2d3462aebfa
except a few mentionned below.

- I have merged their 'rdprail-shell' folder with the 'desktop-shell'
  because they basically copy/pasted 'desktop-shell' and modified it
  slightly to make 'rdprail-shell'. This reduces duplicated code by so
  much that I think it's worth it. To differentiate between the two, a
  shell->rail flag is used in quite a bunch of places.

ARE NOT INCLUDED:
  - the "wslgd-notify" plugin isn't included. This is too much
    WSL-specific.
  - the changes to compositor/rdpdisp.c (new files, not to be conflicted
    with libweston/backend-rdp/rdpdisp.c). Those added multi-monitor layer
    support. This wasn't working out of the box, so it should be
    imported later.
  - the changes to audio / clipboard: those have been integrated back in
    other ways.

